menu "C5VRX buzzer"

config C5VRX_BUZZER_SWEEP
    bool "Sweep the 5 GHz band continuously"
    default y
    help
        Tune through the standard 5 GHz Wi-Fi channels (36..64, 100..144,
        149..177, i.e. 5180..5885 MHz in 20 MHz steps) over and over, measure
        the carrier power on each and drive the buzzer from the strongest
        channel. Disable to listen on C5VRX_BUZZER_WIFI_CHANNEL only.

config C5VRX_BUZZER_SWEEP_MIN_MHZ
    int "Sweep start (MHz)"
    depends on C5VRX_BUZZER_SWEEP
    range 5170 5925
    default 5180
    help
        Lowest channel centre to include. FPV bands live in 5645..5945 MHz;
        5645 skips the Wi-Fi-only lower half and doubles the sweep rate.

config C5VRX_BUZZER_SWEEP_MAX_MHZ
    int "Sweep end (MHz)"
    depends on C5VRX_BUZZER_SWEEP
    range 5170 5925
    default 5925
    help
        Highest channel centre to include. 5885 (channel 177) is the top of
        the standard Wi-Fi grid; 5905 and 5925 (channels 181, 185, FPV bands
        E8 / R8) are offered to the driver as well. Channels the driver
        rejects are reported at boot and skipped.

config C5VRX_BUZZER_SWEEP_STEP_MHZ
    int "Sweep step (MHz)"
    depends on C5VRX_BUZZER_SWEEP
    range 20 40
    default 20
    help
        20 visits every standard channel (the ~20 MHz analog passband then
        covers the band without gaps), 40 visits every other channel for a
        faster sweep.

config C5VRX_BUZZER_WIFI_CHANNEL
    int "5 GHz Wi-Fi channel when not sweeping"
    range 36 177
    default 169
    help
        The receiver starts on this channel and stays on it when the sweep
        is disabled or when every sweep channel is rejected. Centre frequency
        is 5000 + 5 * channel MHz: FPV Raceband R6 5843 MHz -> 169 (5845 MHz),
        band A1 5865 MHz -> 173. C5VRX itself was proven on 173.

config C5VRX_BUZZER_REJECT_NOISE
    bool "Ignore carriers with a noise-like envelope (pure-noise jammers)"
    default y
    help
        An FM video carrier has a constant envelope; Gaussian noise does
        not (power variance / mean^2 close to 1). Channels that fail this
        test never drive the buzzer. Applied only to channels strong enough
        to judge (minimum window power >= 6, about 6 dB above the noise).

config C5VRX_BUZZER_REQUIRE_SYNC
    bool "Require television line sync in the demodulated signal"
    default y
    help
        FM-demodulate the captured I/Q and require the autocorrelation at
        one video line (64.0 us PAL / 63.6 us NTSC) to exceed 0.25. Rejects
        unmodulated (CW), noise-modulated and swept jammers, and also a
        transmitter with no camera attached. Costs about 2 ms per channel
        above the noise. Applied only to channels strong enough to judge.

config C5VRX_BUZZER_GPIO
    int "Buzzer GPIO"
    range 0 28
    default 25
    help
        GPIO that drives the passive buzzer with an LEDC PWM tone.
        25 is pad D2 of the Seeed Studio XIAO ESP32-C5; 3 is its MTDI pad.
        It must not be one of the MODEM_DIAG lane GPIOs 1, 0, 23, 7, 10, 5,
        24 and 4 (see rf.c), which toggle at 40 MHz while receiving.

endmenu
